 "apply_requirements": [
  {
   "id": "remove_nvidia_camera_mount",
   "required": true,
   "what": "Remove NVIDIA's camera-mount model from the robot in the env: make the visual prim <Robot>/gripper/visuals/camera_mount invisible and disable collision on every collider under <Robot>/gripper/collisions/camera_mount, with a mode='prestartup' EventTerm (de-instance the enclosing instanceable prim first). Ready-made function: remove_nvidia_mount() in scripts/check_wrist_mount.py. The collider part belongs in CubeInCupEnvCfg (all variants), the visual part at least in CubeInCupCamEnvCfg.",
   "why": "The mount occupies y = 24..84 mm, z = -56..-18 mm of the gripper frame, directly in front of the fitted camera: with it visible the fitted camera images only the mount (all 307200 px at 2-3 cm depth, first Isaac run). The real camera sees the jaws through that space, so the real arm has nothing there and the collider is a phantom obstacle next to the jaws.",
   "evidence": {
    "isaac_check_with_mount_visible": "scratchpad wrist_mount/isaac_check_1.log: fitted camera 'jaw pixels 307200 (depth [0.0218, 0.0330])'",
    "this_validation": {
     "visual_path": "gripper/visuals/camera_mount",
     "visual_visibility_after_startup": "invisible",
     "collider_path": "gripper/collisions/camera_mount",
     "collision_enabled_after_startup": {
      "gripper/collisions/camera_mount/Cube/Cube": false,
      "gripper/collisions/camera_mount/Cylinder/Cylinder": false
     },
     "removal_event": {
      "visuals_hidden": 1,
      "colliders_disabled": 2,
      "missing": []
     }
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "wrist_intrinsics",
   "required": true,
   "what": "Make the sim render the same pinhole the real frames are undistorted to. Pick ONE: (b) env_cfg: scene.wrist_cam.spawn.distortion = sim_utils.OpenCvPinholeDistortionCfg(fx, fy, cx, cy from WRIST_K, image_size=(640, 480), apply_lens_distortion=False) -> Isaac renders the exact K and the documented real-side cv2.undistort(img, K, DIST) stays valid; (a) keep the default spawn and undistort real frames with cv2.undistort(img, K, DIST, None, K_sim), K_sim = intrinsics.K_isaac_render, and correct the comment in so101_r2s2r/calib.py; (c) change nothing else and use WRIST_CAM_QUAT_KSIM_COMPENSATED instead of WRIST_CAM_QUAT (approximation, see ksim_compensated).",
   "why": "PinholeCameraCfg.from_intrinsic_matrix drops the principal point and averages fx, fy (isaaclab.utils.sensors.convert_camera_intrinsics_to_usd): Isaac renders K_sim (f 550.57, c (320, 240)) while the real K has c (327.54, 246.31), a 7.5 / 6.3 px (0.78 / 0.66 deg) shift. With the pose alone, the sim jaws sit ~7 px off the K-undistorted real jaws.",
   "evidence": {
    "default_spawn_vs_real_undistorted_to_K": 0.815,
    "default_spawn_vs_real_undistorted_to_K_sim_option_a": 0.973,
    "exact_K_spawn_vs_real_undistorted_to_K_option_b": 0.974,
